# Cloudflare Pages version of _redirects.
# Swap this over the root _redirects ONLY at cutover (see CUTOVER.md).
# Do not put this at the repo root while the site is still on Netlify.
#
# Two differences from the Netlify file:
#
# 1. No "!" force flag. Netlify needs 301! to beat an existing file at that
#    path; Cloudflare Pages has no such flag and a bare "301" is correct.
#
# 2. No .html rules. Cloudflare Pages does the .html -> clean-URL redirect
#    natively: /services/iskurit.html -> /services/iskurit and
#    /blog/index.html -> /blog/ are automatic. The 40 .html lines in the
#    Netlify file are therefore unnecessary here.
#    verify_redirects.py proves this against the preview URL before cutover.
#
# What is left is the one redirect Cloudflare cannot infer: the retired
# /privacy path, which must land on /privacy-policy.

/privacy.html   /privacy-policy   301
/privacy        /privacy-policy   301
